   "evidence": "Overlattice/Index.lean:238-239 statement mentions only `AddSubgroup L.DiscriminantGroup`; sibling lemmas that do talk about the correspondence carry the object in the name (`index_eq_natCard_discriminantSubgroup` line 212, `relIndex_eq_relIndex_discriminantSubgroup` line 198).",
   "file": "TauCeti/LinearAlgebra/IntegralLattice/Overlattice/Index.lean",
   "fix": "Move it out of `IntermediateCarrier` into `IntegralLattice` and name the objects, e.g. `IntegralLattice.natCard_mul_relIndex_discriminantSubgroup`; the neighbours `discriminantSubgroup`/`intermediateCarrierOfDiscriminantSubgroup` live in `IntegralLattice` (Overlattice/Basic.lean:92,126).",
   "issue": "`IntermediateCarrier.natCard_mul_relIndex : Nat.card H * H.relIndex K = Nat.card K` states nothing about intermediate carriers \u2014 `H K : AddSubgroup L.DiscriminantGroup` \u2014 yet it sits in the `IntermediateCarrier` namespace (opened at line 88) under a name that mentions neither the discriminant group nor any carrier, so it reads as a general subgroup fact.",
   "line": "238"
  },
  {
   "evidence": "Every `isUnimodular_iff_\u2026` in Unimodular.lean names the full RHS Prop: `isUnimodular_iff_discriminant_eq_one` (line 170, used in the proof at Index.lean:314), `isUnimodular_iff_natCard_discriminantGroup_eq_one` (line 85), `isUnimodular_iff_natAbs_gramDet_eq_one` (line 184).",
   "file": "TauCeti/LinearAlgebra/IntegralLattice/Overlattice/Index.lean",
   "fix": "Rename to `isUnimodular_iff_index_sq_eq_discriminant` and `isUnimodular_iff_natCard_sq_eq_discriminant`.",
   "issue": "`IsIntegral.isUnimodular_iff_index_sq` names only `index_sq` for a right-hand side that is the equation `index M ^ 2 = L.discriminant`; the name reads as if the RHS were a property of the index squared. Same defect at line 334, `IsIntegral.isUnimodular_iff_natCard_sq` (`Nat.card H ^ 2 = L.discriminant`).",
   "line": "304"
  }
